## Backend targeting

- **StreamPulse website / portal (`streampulse-web`, `/analytics`, website portal docs) uses hosted API by default:** `https://api.streampulse.stream`.
- Never switch portal dev, QA screenshots, hub checks, or emote verification to `http://localhost:8090` unless the user explicitly asks for local-stack debugging. Local `:8090` is the Streamclone developer stack and usually has a tiny/non-representative IRC pool.
- Before portal work, check `streampulse-web/.env.development.local`, `/setup`, and `sessionStorage.sp.backendUrlOverride`; if any points at `localhost:8090`, switch back to hosted or warn before relying on hub/moment/emote data.
- Local `http://localhost:8090` is only for Streamclone backend implementation, extension local testing, and explicit `/v1/extension/*` smoke checks.
- **Hosted production promotion** is not the Streamclone registry path: see streamclone [`production-promotion-contract.md`](../../../twitch-7tv-clone/docs/production-promotion-contract.md) and [image exit audit](../../docs/pulse-extension/evidence/streamclone-image-exit-audit-2026-07.md). Pre-cutover private ops may still pin `streamclone/*` source images.
- Content scripts: `chrome.runtime.sendMessage` only — no `fetch`.
- **Analytics surfaces:** no new `rgba(255,255,255,…)` backgrounds on cards, rows, chips, or panels under `streampulse-web/src/ui/components/analytics`. Use `--sp-surface-*` tokens from `streampulse-web/src/ui/themes/analytics-surfaces.css`.
- **Hub landing (`/analytics`):** readability reformat only — real sidebar anchors, honest KPIs from `/v1/public/hub`, no mock-only/disabled nav, no duplicate live rail + tracked table + trust pipeline blocks.
- **Hub Pulse Moments (embedded):** table + side **Moment inspector** stay side-by-side; KPI row is one line (Emotes/Chat/Viewers); **Selected minute emotes** fills the remaining side-column height. Do not put moment inspector in the chart rail on hub landing. Layout contract: [`docs/website-portal/analytics-command-center-layout.md`](../../docs/website-portal/analytics-command-center-layout.md).
- **Chart rail inspector:** default footer is **Top live by activity**; bucket modes use **Top streamers this bucket** with optimistic live-pool streamers on click (no blank wait). Do not remove range footer or revert to provider mix.
